From c881fe15ff6e1b3821a55caba2aab286465912cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iamwrm <iamwrm@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 12:52:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] feat(client): mirror the terminal-ansi frame stream in
 a screen model

Predictive local echo (i0002 W3) needs the terminal-ansi client to know
what is on screen: cursor position, cell contents, and whether a cell is
unstyled. New src/client/screen_model.rs replays received TerminalFrame
bytes into a cell grid.

The frame stream comes exclusively from BlitEncoder, whose vocabulary is
small and has no scrolling or relative cursor motion - every cell write is
preceded by an absolute CUP, so a printable run between escapes is exactly
one cell's grapheme cluster. The parser covers CUP, SGR (tracking only
plain-vs-styled pen), 2J, ?25h/l, ?2026 sync, DECSCUSR, OSC 8 hyperlinks
(cells under a link are not plain), OSC 52 and Kitty APC passthrough.
apply() reports touched cells for prediction reconciliation.

Round-trip tests validate the model against real BlitEncoder output (full
and diff frames, wide chars, hyperlinks, hidden cursor). Not wired into
the client loop yet; the prediction engine lands separately.
